{"q":"94","t":"Binary Tree Inorder Traversal","d":"Easy","p":false,"c":"<p>Given the <code>root</code> of a binary tree, return <em>the inorder traversal of its nodes&#39; values</em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,null,2,3]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[1,3,2]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/302bbb22b40631ca.png\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 264px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1,2,3,4,5,null,8,null,null,6,7,9]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[4,2,6,5,7,1,3,9,8]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/assets/img/1c2fff4664fdf9e0.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 286px;\" /></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = []</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[]</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 4:</strong></p>\n\n<div class=\"example-block\">\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">root = [1]</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> <span class=\"example-io\">[1]</span></p>\n</div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>The number of nodes in the tree is in the range <code>[0, 100]</code>.</li>\n\t<li><code>-100 &lt;= Node.val &lt;= 100</code></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<strong>Follow up:</strong> Recursive solution is trivial, could you do it iteratively?","h":[],"m":"{\r\n  \"name\": \"inorderTraversal\",\r\n  \"params\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"root\",\r\n      \"type\": \"TreeNode\"\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"return\": {\r\n    \"type\": \"list<integer>\",\r\n    \"dealloc\": true\r\n  }\r\n}","g":[{"name":"Stack","slug":"stack"},{"name":"Tree","slug":"tree"},{"name":"Depth-First Search","slug":"depth-first-search"},{"name":"Binary Tree","slug":"binary-tree"}],"s":[{"t":"Validate Binary Search Tree","s":"validate-binary-search-tree","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Binary Tree Preorder Traversal","s":"binary-tree-preorder-traversal","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Binary Tree Postorder Traversal","s":"binary-tree-postorder-traversal","d":"Easy","p":false},{"t":"Binary Search Tree Iterator","s":"binary-search-tree-iterator","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Kth Smallest Element in a BST","s":"kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Closest Binary Search Tree Value II","s":"closest-binary-search-tree-value-ii","d":"Hard","p":false},{"t":"Inorder Successor in BST","s":"inorder-successor-in-bst","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Convert Binary Search Tree to Sorted Doubly Linked List","s":"convert-binary-search-tree-to-sorted-doubly-linked-list","d":"Medium","p":false},{"t":"Minimum Distance Between BST Nodes","s":"minimum-distance-between-bst-nodes","d":"Easy","p":false}],"co":[["Google","google"],["Amazon","amazon"],["Meta","facebook"],["Anduril","anduril"],["Bloomberg","bloomberg"],["Microsoft","microsoft"],["tcs","tcs"]],"cs":{"a":[["Google","google",11],["Amazon","amazon",7],["Meta","facebook",2],["Bloomberg","bloomberg",2],["Anduril","anduril",2]],"b":[],"m":[["Microsoft","microsoft",14],["tcs","tcs",2]]}}